  "body": "Fork synced at v0.19.0; branched from upstream/main 7bfb1824 (after #1585 merged).\n\n## What changed\n- `depth_law_of` (`crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`): `OpParams::TrochoidalSlot` joins the Slot and Circular arm, `Slot | TrochoidalSlot | Circular => authored_law(src)`, still after the `part_solid` early return. An Entity or Selection source naming the finished part is `DepthLaw::Section`; a Stock source (or a pick off the setup's stock) still cuts unjudged.\n- #1513's `slot_fit::refuse_unfit_slot` is unchanged. A picked slot that does not fit its region in XY is still refused at generate. The new law adds the depth check, and on a whole model the walls, which the fit check never read.\n- **Root cause:** TrochoidalSlot fell to `_ => DepthLaw::None`, so nothing on the operation judged its hand-typed endpoints and width. `uncovered()` (posting_sim.rs) counts any fresh, stamped op as judged, so the post relied on the program sim alone. The sim refuses to judge a turned stock, and it missed the through-wall case even with the stock aligned.\n- Doc comments, `authored_law_tests.rs` and `docs/decisions/1593-trochoid-law.md` (decision plus an audit of the other kinds) are updated.\n\n## Other 2D kinds still at `None` on a part-solid source (audit)\nProbed on the same fixture, with a whole-model source cut to Z1:\n- **Pocket / Adaptive2D / Offset2D, whole model:** left as is. By contract the source is the volume to remove. Every move below the floor stays outside the part (radius 23+ against the 20 mm half-block), and the program sim agrees. Picks were already `Section`.\n- **Chamfer2D:** left as is. It enters the part by design, and its depth is derived, not typed.\n- **Engrave / Trace:** left at `None` (Section would convict legal engravings). They are **filed as P1 #1595**: cut to Z1 on a whole model, they run 3-7 mm under the model. The aligned program sim refuses that, and with the stock turned it posts.\n- **Drill with cross holes:** this is the lathe turret's cross drill, judged by its own laws, not a 2D mill kind.\n\nThis table is pinned by `the_kinds_that_enter_or_remove_the_part_by_contract_stay_unjudged`.\n\n## Pins (`crates/app/tests/trochoid_law.rs`, fixture: 40x40x8 block, R15 pocket to Z4, 6 mm EM; all go through generate, then verify, then post)\n- `a_whole_model_trochoid_through_the_pocket_wall_gouges_and_never_posts`: x 4..20, 10 wide, at the floor. With the stock aligned **and** turned, the op has gouges and `post_setup` refuses with \"T1: move N cuts past the finish surface\". No file is written.\n- `a_whole_model_trochoid_under_the_floor_gouges_and_never_posts_where_the_sim_cannot_judge`: 3 mm under the floor. With the stock turned, the post is refused on the op's own gouge. With it aligned, the op gouges and the post is refused (the sim's clause leads the message).\n- `a_picked_trochoid_that_fits_its_floor_but_sinks_under_it_never_posts`: a floor pick that fits in XY, 3 mm deep, stock turned. The post is refused on the op's gouge.\n- `a_trochoid_inside_the_pocket_at_its_floor_stays_clean_and_posts`: no blocking finding on either stock, and it posts on the aligned one.\n- `a_trochoid_on_the_stock_is_never_judged`: a `SrcRef::Stock` source and a pick on the from-model stock's floor both get 0 gouges.\n- `over_mcp_the_whole_model_trochoid_is_judged_the_same`: `add_operation` \"Trochoidal slot\" with source \"part\", then `verify`. The wall case gives op gouges with `ok:false`; the legal case gives `ok:true`.\n- Unit tests: `the_trochoidal_slot_answers_to_the_same_authored_law`, the audit table above, and TrochoidalSlot added to `a_source_that_is_not_the_part_is_never_judged`.\n\n| mutation (each alone, then reverted) | trochoid_law result |\n|---|---|\n| M1 TrochoidalSlot arm removed (back to `None`, the pre-fix code) | red: wall, under-floor, picked, MCP (4) |\n| M2 `authored_law` Entity -> None | red: wall, under-floor, MCP (3) |\n| M3 `authored_law` Selection -> None | red: picked (1) |\n| M4 `part_solid` early return disabled | red: stock never judged (1) |\n| M5 verify `gouge_tol` -> -0.05 (over-conviction) | red: legal stays clean, MCP legal, stock (3) |\n| tightening `contain_into`'s allowance | survives; that is the Contain kinds' law, never reached by Section, so it is equivalent here |\n\nGoldens unchanged: golden_cl 32 passed, solid_law_goldens passed. trochoid_confine (#1503/#1513) and trochoid_op pass.\n\n## Gate\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green on 5482f653 (app suites 716 s, ui suites 47 s, 0 failed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\nA tilted-frame (`Some(frame)`) Trochoidal slot on a part source has no dedicated pin; the framed branch feeds the local model to `Section` the same way it does for the Circular.\n\nChangelog: A Trochoidal slot on the finished part (whole model or pick) is now judged against it: a channel typed through a wall or below the floor is a blocking gouge on the operation and the post is refused, even where the program sim cannot judge (#1593).\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1593\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
